  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 110 AM Monday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...  Dry and seasonable weather continues through the \nweek. The first day of November could bring some rain.\n\nThe quiet weather that has been in place over central North Carolina \nfor the last week is expected to continue for several more days. \nSome additional cloud cover is likely on Wednesday as a weak front \npasses over Virginia, but otherwise, do not expect much change to \nthe ongoing pattern. There will be a minimal warming trend towards \nthe end of the week. Models are suggesting that a chance of rain \ncould finally return to the forecast on Sunday, November 1, but \nuntil then, there simply doesn't appear to be any chance of breaking \nthe ongoing dry stretch.",
